# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# utils/ — vendored engines & third-party sandboxes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KEEP only the SOURCE the app / build actually uses:
#   llama.cpp      local inference engine source (config_loader default
#                  "utils/llama.cpp"); run_looper.bat builds it locally and its
#                  outputs (utils/llama.cpp/build*, *.exe/*.dll) are ignored.
#   nano-graphrag  Graph RAG (added to the PyInstaller pathex)
#   rdpwrap        RDP sandbox bootstrap (LoOper/setup_rdp_agent.py)
#
# Engine/models are NOT committed - run_looper.bat fetches them at setup:
#   Laya models  -> LoOper/AI/models/laya-GGUF/   (HF: mys/laya-GGUF)
#   Laya engine  -> LoOper/AI/bin/laya.exe        (ggmlc release zip)
# Everything below is an unrelated sandbox / upstream mirror / fetched asset
# and is NOT referenced anywhere in LoOper source or the build pipeline.
/utils/.cache/

/utils/ComoRAG/
/utils/NodeEditTestCPP/
/utils/Stop-RAG/
/utils/aider/
/utils/ggmlc/
/utils/laya-GGUF/
/utils/little-coder/
/utils/llama.cpp.upstream/
/utils/openjev/
/utils/playwright-mcp/
/utils/stop/
/utils/laya_english_f16.gguf
/utils/license.bin
/utils/blockkey/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .qoder — agent workspace (scratch files, caches, ~2 GB test blobs)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.qoder/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets & private artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
keygen/private_key.pem
keygen/validate_license_build.py
*license_validator.spec
.env
.env.*

